rs: createText (loads fonts first), color consts, cloneIcon(name), setIconColor, etc. That's fine but verbose. Keep helpers compact.\n\nAlso node persistence: I can find nodes by name on the workspace page between calls. Good: store component main nodes at known x positions.\n\nMedia icon components: figma.getNodeById works after switching current page? Earlier the first call returned empty objects — but that was because I ran code without switching pages and possibly because getNodeById returned null and my inspect threw? Actually it returned \"{}\" — the inspect returned object with only... wait it returned {\"button\":{}} meaning inspect(btn) returned {} — so btn was defined (not null) but properties were all undefined? That happens if the node wasn't loaded (page not current). After switching page it worked. Since media components are on page 1:4, and I need them while building on page 8:2 — components can be instanced from any page via createInstance regardless of current page, and getNodeById should work after any page is loaded. To be safe: at the start of each call, do `await figma.setCurrentPageAsync(workspacePage)` then getNodeById for media components — earlier failure suggests cross-page access failed when current page was 0:1 and node was on 1:3. Hmm, actually maybe it failed because I never awaited setCurrentPage at all and the default current page was the first page; nodes on other pages return null from getNodeById? It returned {} not error, so btn was a truthy object... possibly a \"null-ish\" dead node proxy. Anyway: to access media components reliably, I might need setCurrentPageAsync(mediaPage) first to load it, then switch to workspace. I'll do: switch to media page, grab references? References may go stale when switching pages... In Figma plugin API, node references remain valid across page switches within one execution. The real issue: pages must be \"loaded\" — in plugins all pages are always loaded; getNodeById works globally. The earlier em