{"type":"assistant","message":{"type":"message","model":"kimi-k3","usage":{"input_tokens":102036,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_5_m_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_1_h_tokens":0},"role":"assistant","id":"02036ae523520a7a0574a143cc71777d","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Screens look decent. Issue: icons render as solid squares (the media icon instances render as filled squares, not glyphs). Earlier the screenshot of 03 showed header icons as squares too. Why? recolor(node,color) replaces fills with solid color — but icons show as SQUARES, meaning the vector itself is square? No — the media icons are components with vector children. When instanced and recolored they should keep glyph shape. But in screenshots they render as solid squares 24x24.\n\nWait — maybe the icon component's vector child has its own fills but ALSO there's a background rect? Let me inspect Icon_Menu (2:50) structure. Earlier probe of 2:27 showed children: [{t:'VECTOR', f:'SOLID{...}'}] — a single vector. Rendering as square suggests the vector's geometry fills the 24x24 box... unless the resize(24,24) distorted? No, icons are 24x24 originally.\n\nHmm, but screenshot 03 shows menu icon as a dark square. Perhaps the icons in media are displayed in the library as glyphs, but when I resize an instance that contains vectors with constraints... resize should be fine.\n\nActually wait — maybe the recolor function overwrote fills of a FRAME wrapper with solid, and frames render as filled rectangles covering children! In headerIcon: icon() → mediaInst creates instance i; recolor(i,color) sets fills on ALL nodes with fills INCLUDING the instance root (INSTANCE) itself. Setting fills on an instance root paints the whole instance bounding box as a solid rect behind/over children! Instance fills property — setting fills on an instance/frame adds a background fill to the frame → renders as solid square.\n\nYes! That's it. My recolor sets node.fills on every node including container frames/instances. For the status bar (6:32) recolor sets its fill to white → fine visually (bg) but also covers... wait status bar instance root fill was SOLID initially (bg). For icon instances, the root instance probably has fills=[] originally — but my check `node.fills.length` requires length>0... For the icon instance root, fills likely = [] (no fill), so it's skipped, and only vector children (which have solid fills) get recolored. Hmm, then icons should render as glyphs.\n\nBut screenshots show squares. So maybe the icon component root itself HAS a solid fill (a 24x24 bounding box fill, e.g. white or the dark #1A1A1F). The probe earlier: children of 2:27 = one VECTOR with solid fill #1A1A1F-ish. The component root may also have fills. My recolor would then repaint component root fill → square in chosen color.\n\nLet me inspect an instance as created in s3 to see. Simplest: fix recolor to skip INSTANCE/FRAME/COMPONENT roots and only paint VECTOR/ELLIPSE/RECTANGLE-with-vector... but status bar contains RECTANGLE children (signal bars) that need recolor; the Battery frame root might have fill too.\n\nNew approach for recolor: only set fills on nodes whose type is VECTOR or STAR or POLYGON or ELLIPSE or RECTANGLE... but rectangles inside status bar are the signal bars (want colored). The Home Indicator child Rectangle = the bar (want colored). Battery frame contains Rectangle (want colored). OK: color LEAF shapes only (VECTOR, ELLIPSE, RECTANGLE, STAR, POLYGON, LINE) — but the Home Indicator root itself is a component with fillType SOLID (its own bg?) — its child rect is the indicator bar.\n\nWait, but icon squares: the square IS probably a vector (icons built with a bounding-box vector that has fill?). Probe showed ONE child vector with solid fill. If that vector is the glyph, recoloring it is right and it should look like a glyph. But it renders as a square!\n\nHmm — maybe the issue: when I resize the instance from its original size to 24x24... icons were already 24x24. No.\n\nOR the real issue: my recolor on the INSTANCE root. Instance roots can have fills. The probe earlier was on the COMPONENT (2:27) children, not the instance root. If the component itself has fills=[SOLID dark] (a bounding rect fill as background), the instance inherits it, and my recolor changes it — but even without recolor it would render as dark square. Let me check 2:27's own fills.\n\nActually the status bar showed correctly? In 02 screenshot, status bar = dark navy band with white... I saw a navy band at top with a tiny white square top-right — battery rendered as square! The whole status bar looks like a plain navy strip without time/icons visible. Because recolor set fills on the status bar INSTANCE ROOT and all children INCLUDING the 'Signal' FRAME and 'Battery' FRAME roots — frame roots with fills=[] skipped, but vector/rect leaves colored white — that should be fine... The time '9:41' text has fills (TEXT type) — my recolor condition 'fills' in node && SOLID applies to TEXT too → text colored white — good. But screenshot shows no 9:41. Hmm, maybe time text was colored white on navy and... it's there? Screenshot 01 top: black band with nothing visible except... Actually in screenshot 01, the top band looks solid black/navy, no 9:41, no battery except... there IS a small square top-right in 02's status bar (white square = battery filled white square?).\n\nI think the status bar instance root has a solid fill (white bg?) — no wait, the band renders NAVY (#10122B ink). That's because the instance root got recolored to ink! Root fill=ink → whole 390x44 rect ink → covers children (children render above root fill actually; children are drawn ON TOP of root fill). Then Signal frame: I set fills on frame root? If Signal frame has fills=[] skipped. Wifi is ELLIPSE → colored. Battery frame root skipped; its Rectangle child colored. Time text colored. So we should see white glyphs on ink band... but