so we'd see glyph in ink over ink square... root is a full 24x24 rect → solid square!). Yes! The instance root has a white RECT-like fill (the icon component root itself has a white fill = full frame). I set it to ink → solid ink square behind/around the glyph. The vector glyph on top is also ink → invisible against it. Result: solid square.\n\nFix: instance ROOT fill must be transparent/white-none, vector gets the color. My second paint run: checked `c.r>0.9` root white → root was already recolored to ink/mute (not white) → skipped. That's why nothing changed.\n\nFix now: for icon instances (24x24 or similar with single vector child), set instance root fills=[] and vector fills to intended color. But what color? I overwrote original intent: active vs inactive distinction is lost — I can recover from the TEXT LABEL color in the same tab (label fill = primary if active). Similarly header icons: intended ink on light, white on dark, primary in tint chips.\n\nStrategy: walk every icon INSTANCE; determine target color by context:\n- If parent chip frame has tint fill (tint color) → primary.\n- Else if screen is a trade screen or 02/06 (dark bg) → near-white.\n- Else → ink.\n- For nav tabs: use the sibling text label's fill color.\n\nSimpler: set vector fill = instance current fill (which holds the intended color from build-time recolor!), then instance root fills=[]. Since build-time recolor set BOTH root and vector to the same intended color, the current instance fill IS the intended color. \n\nAlso for shell instances: root fills=[] done? My first fix set node.fills=[] for shell and black children→color, and returned fixed 16 (probably from shell children + some). Verify shell now.\n\nThen also fix 03 header icons etc. Implement: for every INSTANCE in screens that has a direct VECTOR child and root fill SOLID non-white-ish... just do universally: if instance has vector descendants and root has SOLID fill: if root fill alpha/white — regardless: set vector fills to root